From c239696bbd05571b45a29c2fad1e48cbad3869fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:51:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][VideoPlayer] Take the settings of a film from an
 add-on again from any source

With "Remember the settings of films from add-ons" (Player > Videos, on
by default), a film or an episode with ids of its own, not of the
library, that an add-on plays (an add-on's path, or a stream from the
internet: add-ons play such links with Player.play() or
setResolvedUrl(), with the IMDb and TMDb ids of the film, or of the show
with the season and number of the episode) keeps its settings by what it
is, not by its link:
- the player names it when it prepares the file; once the demuxer is
  open and the settings kept for its path were given to it (the queue of
  the callbacks is waited for, 5 s at most, so they never come after),
  the callback reads its records and gives the settings to start with,
  before the streams are chosen; when it closes, what the user chose is
  kept as the record of that release (FilmMemory.h);
- subtitles that were turned off stay off; a subtitle choice that the new
  source cannot meet is left to the settings, as for a video without one;
- the Dolby Vision output chosen for it (DVOutputMemory.h) is kept by its
  ids too, and checked against its stream as before;
- a short notification says what was restored, and the log what was
  taken from which playback and what was not, and why.
Files on this device and on the local network, discs and items of the
library keep their settings for their path or file, as in Kodi.
